# Backend Module Structure (Responsibility-Based)

Split modules by **responsibility** (what the code does), not by audience (who calls it).

## Folder Layout

```
<module>/
├── <module>.module.ts
├── controllers/
│   ├── <module>.controller.ts                    ← core CRUD
│   ├── <module>-<responsibility>.controller.ts   ← heavy sub-domain (5+ endpoints)
│   ├── <module>-self.controller.ts               ← "my" data (actor-scoped reads)
│   └── bulk-<module>.controller.ts               ← file upload, async jobs, SSE
├── services/
│   ├── <module>.service.ts                       ← shared queries + core logic
│   ├── <module>-<responsibility>.service.ts      ← sub-domain logic
│   └── bulk-<module>.service.ts                  ← batch processing
└── dto/
    ├── <module>.dto.ts                           ← base response + base input DTOs
    ├── <module>-<responsibility>.dto.ts          ← sub-domain DTOs
    ├── <audience>-<module>.dto.ts                ← audience-specific inputs (when shapes differ)
    └── bulk-<module>.dto.ts                      ← batch DTOs
```

## When to Split

```
Sub-area has 5+ endpoints with distinct logic?
  → Responsibility-split: controller + service  (e.g. placement-compliance)

Just "my view" of the same data?
  → Self-split: controller only, SAME service   (e.g. placement-self)

File upload / async jobs / SSE streaming?
  → Bulk-split: controller + service            (e.g. bulk-users)

Audience has different input shape but same logic?
  → Audience DTO only, no extra service          (e.g. vendor-user.dto.ts)

Audience has different input shape AND different logic?
  → Audience controller + service               (e.g. vendor-users)
```

### When NOT to Split

- Controller has < 10 methods → one file
- Sub-area has < 5 endpoints → keep in core controller
- "Self" has 1-2 reads → keep in core controller
- Bulk is just "loop and call create" → single endpoint in relevant controller

## Examples

### Placements (responsibility-split + self-split)

```
placements/
  controllers/
    placements.controller.ts              ← CRUD + notes + tasks + history
    placement-compliance.controller.ts    ← submit/review/bulk-add compliance items
    placement-self.controller.ts          ← "my placements" (candidate/vendor reads)
  services/
    placements.service.ts                 ← shared queries, core logic
    placement-compliance.service.ts       ← compliance-specific logic
  dto/
    placement.dto.ts
    placement-compliance.dto.ts
```

### Users (audience-split + bulk-split)

```
users/
  controllers/
    users.controller.ts                   ← common lookups (MSP options)
    program-users.controller.ts           ← admin CRUD
    vendor-users.controller.ts            ← vendor portal CRUD (different route, logic, DTOs)
    bulk-users.controller.ts              ← CSV import, job streaming
  services/
    users.service.ts                      ← shared queries
    program-users.service.ts              ← admin user logic + CASL checks
    vendor-users.service.ts               ← vendor-scoped logic + actor resolution
    bulk-users.service.ts                 ← file upload, background jobs
  dto/
    user.dto.ts                           ← base response + base input
    program-user.dto.ts                   ← extends base (role, status, mspId)
    vendor-user.dto.ts                    ← standalone (fullName, departmentId)
    bulk-users.dto.ts                     ← wraps audience DTO in array
```

## Service Dependency Direction

```
bulk service       ──→ core service (reuses single-item methods)
responsibility svc ──→ core service (shared queries/helpers)
self controller    ──→ core service (direct, no intermediate service)
audience service   ──→ core service + other domain services
```

Only the core service is exported from the module for cross-module use.

## DTO Strategy

- **Extend** base DTO when audience adds fields on top of the same shape
- **Standalone** DTO when audience shape diverges (different field names/types)
- **Query DTOs** extend `PaginatedQueryDto`; live in the sub-domain's DTO file

## Authorization

- **Controller**: `@Permissions({ action, subject })` — coarse CASL gate
- **Service**: fine-grained rules — actor resolution, role assertions, self-action prevention
- Subjects stay generic (`"User"`, `"Placement"`) — not per-responsibility or per-audience

## Module Registration

One `<module>.module.ts` registers all controllers/services. One import in `app.module.ts` per domain — no separate modules for sub-domains or audiences.
